UPSERT source:hud_recon_dump_impl SET kind='implementation',
  ref='web/render-replica/replay.html renderHudPass (browser); web/render-replica/hud-client.mjs drawHUD/_lifeBar/_meter/renderPlatesOnly; core/network/maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp ~3543 (dump companions); core/network/maplecast_mirror.cpp:4052 gstaBuildHudTA (NATIVE client HUD).',
  note='Browser HUD fix landed + compiles N/A (JS). Part B compiles NINJA_EXIT=0 (object built, not yet relinked — PID 62532 holds the exe lock). Native-client HUD is a SEPARATE larger port, scoped not shipped.';

-- PART A: browser HUD now reconstruct-from-state; HUDQ pass-through DROPPED (issue 3).
UPSERT finding:hud_reconstruct_from_state_browser SET
  statement='IMPLEMENTED (browser replay.html), pending live verify. renderHudPass() previously early-returned into renderHudQuads() (the engine HUDQ pass-through) whenever the HUDQ tail was present, suppressing the working state-reconstructed bars -> the issue-3 fill-static symptom (HUDQ life-bar quad x[439..591] constant as p2hp 144->55). FIX: removed the HUDQ early-return; renderHudPass now ALWAYS runs the zero-byte state path: populateHudStateFromRAM() (reads per-slot health 0x420, red_health 0x424, active 0x000, char_id 0x001, meter_fill 0x8C289646/648, lvl 0x8C28964A/64B, timer 0x630, combo 0x670 — ALL already in the read-set) -> SPRITECLIENT.drawHUD(ctx) (life bars hpFrac=health/144 + ROM BAR_COLS loc_8c15FFB0 + red_health chip, meters, timer, combo) -> hud.renderPlatesOnly(ctx) (corner portraits + names by char_id). Dropped the now-dead drawHudReal() call. WHAT EACH ELEMENT RECONSTRUCTS FROM (zero added bytes): bars=health/red_health; meter=meter_fill+lvl; timer=0x630; combo=0x670; portraits/names=char_id+active; win-stars=UNDRAWN (per-side win field is a MISSING wire field, [hud:no-bogus-stars] — empty beats fabricated, unchanged). With HUDQ off for the overlay, MAPLECAST_HUD_TA is DROPPABLE (~30KB/frame saved) once confirmed nothing else consumes HUDQ. NEEDS LIVE-CLIENT VERIFY (drift-captures cannot confirm portraits/stars/glyph coverage): bars track health+meter through a combo, portraits/names present, nothing regressed. re_kb/54.',
  status='implemented', confidence='high', date='2026-06-29';

-- PART A native-client: IMPLEMENTED (STAGED — bars-from-state via HUDQ reshape), live-verify pending.
UPSERT finding:hud_native_client_port_scoped SET
  statement='IMPLEMENTED (STAGED), COMPILES + LINKED (build/flycast.exe relinked NINJA_EXIT=0, fresh PE 20:52), pending USER live verify. The user verifies the NATIVE GSTA client (build/flycast.exe, "Flycast - MapleCast Mirror"), HUD = gstaBuildHudTA (maplecast_mirror.cpp:4052). APPROACH (lowest-risk; the browser drawHUD is Canvas2D and cannot port 1:1 to the TA pipeline): RESHAPE the engine HUDQ HP-fill quad by LIVE health from _gstaRam, NOT a new TA HUD renderer. In the NATIVE client the HUDQ tail and _gstaRam are the SAME wire frame (no GSTA-vs-mirror drift), so rescaling the fill quad inner edge by hpFrac=read8(slotBase+0x420)/144 tracks health correctly. IMPL: detect HP-fill quads by signature (tcw==0x80000, w 100..340, bar-body height 4..14px, top band cy 60..130 — MEASURED _hud_bar_geom.mjs fnum=441: P1 x[48..201]/P2 x[439..591]); map each to its team slot by side (cx<320=>P1) + cy-row (active-first order, top bar=active point char; slots P1=[0,2,4] P2=[1,3,5]); move INNER x-edge toward outer (portrait) anchor so width=full*hpFrac (P1 anchored left, P2 anchored right). CONSERVATIVE: only signature-matching quads reshaped; frame/highlight/portraits/names/meter/timer/combo glyphs pass through HUDQ VERBATIM. ZERO added bytes. STAGED LIMITS (follow-up): (a) METER fill still HUDQ-verbatim (not yet state-reshaped, meter_fill 0x8C289646/648); (b) full reconstruct + HUDQ drop + MAPLECAST_HUD_TA off is the END STATE. Win-stars stay UNDRAWN (missing wire field). NEEDS LIVE VERIFY (offline-unvalidatable): bars track health through a combo, portraits/names present, nothing regressed; if the fill-quad signature mis-detects, the thresholds need a live-tune. re_kb/44.',
  status='implemented', confidence='medium', date='2026-06-29';

-- PART B: frame-exact dump now Windows-complete (additive env overrides).
UPSERT finding:dump_companions_windows_pathable SET
  statement='IMPLEMENTED + COMPILES (NINJA_EXIT=0; object built, relink pending PID-62532 exe lock). maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp dump block: the companion VRAM/PVR/engine-TA outputs were HARDCODED to /dev/shm (MSVC fopen NULL on Windows -> silent skip). ADDED getenv overrides (additive, Linux defaults unchanged): MAPLECAST_DUMP_VRAM_PATH (default /dev/shm/mc_vram_dump.bin), MAPLECAST_DUMP_PVR_PATH (/dev/shm/mc_pvr_regs.bin), MAPLECAST_DUMP_TA_PATH (/dev/shm/mc_engine_ta.bin) + per-file FAILED-to-open stderr so a bad path is visible. With the already-env-pathable MAPLECAST_DUMP_RAM_PATH + the re-armable MAPLECAST_DUMP_RAM_TRIGGER (consumes+removes the trigger file each in-match frame it fires), a Windows headless can now dump RAM+VRAM+PVR+engine-TA at the SAME triggered frame for a ZERO-drift render_frame-vs-engine A/B (unblocks 1a motion-blocks, 5 super stage-garble, 1b Storm transposition). DUMP TRIGGER MECHANISM: set MAPLECAST_DUMP_RAM_TRIGGER=<win-path>; create that file (any C-runtime write to an NTFS path; MSYS touch /dev/shm gives Permission denied); the next in-match frame dumps all 4 + removes the trigger (re-armable). The env-override change is now COMPILED + LINKED into build/flycast.exe (the client relink picked up oracle_hook.cpp too). HEADLESS relink (build-headless-win) intentionally NOT done — PID 62532 holds that exe lock + is the live-verify rig; the headless relink + frame-exact garble dumps (1a/5/1b) are a SEPARATE maintenance window (stop 62532 -> ninja flycast -> relaunch via launch_headless_minimal.cmd which now sets all 4 dump paths -> verify 7212 @ 60fps).',
  status='implemented', confidence='high', date='2026-06-29';

RELATE finding:hud_reconstruct_from_state_browser->cites->source:hud_recon_dump_impl;
